{
  "summary": "The change makes the source generator null-safe for members of closed generic value types defined in referenced assemblies (GetPropertyIdentifierLocation and FirstOrDefault() syntax access), so building no longer crashes with CS8785/AD0001 and a resolver is generated; it also wraps diagnostic reporting in ReportIfLocatedInCompilation to avoid reporting locations outside the compilation being analyzed. The build passes and the three new metadata-reference tests pass. However, ReportIfLocatedInCompilation's condition is inverted (`!ContainsSyntaxTree`), so it drops all diagnostics for types declared in the current compilation and causes 40 newly failing tests (REQ-2283-N1 not met), and tests.fail_without_fix was not run (REQ-2283-N2 unverified). The change should not merge until the filter is corrected.",
  "requirement_verdicts": [
    {
      "req": "REQ-2283-F1",
      "verdict": "met",
      "confidence_basis": "Build passes and the three new metadata-reference tests pass on head, showing no CS8785/AD0001 crash and that the resolver is generated; the null-safety fixes address the crash path. tests.fail_without_fix was not run, so independent confirmation that the tests fail without the fix is missing.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "check", "id": "build", "status": "pass"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 239, "rev": "head", "quote": "this.reportDiagnostic = reportAnalyzerDiagnostic is null ? null : diagnostic => ReportIfLocatedInCompilation(reportAnalyzerDiagnostic, diagnostic);"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 985, "rev": "head", "quote": "this.reportDiagnostic?.Invoke(Diagnostic.Create(MsgPack00xMessagePackAnalyzer.BothStringAndIntKeyAreNull, GetPropertyIdentifierLocation(item), formattedType.ToDisplayString(SymbolDisplayFormat.FullyQualifiedFormat), item.Name));"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1077, "rev": "head", "quote": "Diagnostic.Create(MsgPack00xMessagePackAnalyzer.MemberNeedsKey, item.DeclaringSyntaxReferences.FirstOrDefault()?.GetSyntax().GetLocation()"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "GenericsFormatterTests.ClosedGenericStruct_FromMetadataReference", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "GenericsFormatterTests.ClosedGenericRecordStruct_FromMetadataReference", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "GenericsFormatterTests.ClosedGenericStruct_FromMetadataReference_UnkeyedMember", "outcome": "passed"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2283-F2",
      "verdict": "met",
      "confidence_basis": "The same three new tests pass on head with a verifier that fails on any analyzer diagnostic, demonstrating the analyzer does not throw (no AD0001) for metadata-referenced closed generic value types. tests.fail_without_fix was not run.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "check", "id": "build", "status": "pass"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "GenericsFormatterTests.ClosedGenericStruct_FromMetadataReference", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "GenericsFormatterTests.ClosedGenericRecordStruct_FromMetadataReference", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "GenericsFormatterTests.ClosedGenericStruct_FromMetadataReference_UnkeyedMember", "outcome": "passed"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2283-F3",
      "verdict": "cannot_determine",
      "confidence_basis": "The filter meant to keep diagnostics inside the current compilation has an inverted condition (`!ContainsSyntaxTree`), and the 40 newly failing analyzer tests show in-compilation diagnostics are dropped; correct suppression of out-of-compilation diagnostics cannot be confirmed from the evidence.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 239, "rev": "head", "quote": "this.reportDiagnostic = reportAnalyzerDiagnostic is null ? null : diagnostic => ReportIfLocatedInCompilation(reportAnalyzerDiagnostic, diagnostic);"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1446, "rev": "head", "quote": "if (diagnostic.Location.IsInSource && !this.compilation.ContainsSyntaxTree(diagnostic.Location.SourceTree))"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1448, "rev": "head", "quote": "report(diagnostic);"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "MsgPack00xAnalyzerTests.AddAttributeToType_Fields", "outcome": "failed"},
        {"kind": "check", "id": "tests.full_suite", "status": "fail"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2283-N1",
      "verdict": "not_met",
      "confidence_basis": "tests.full_suite failed: 40 tests newly failing (0 also failing on base), each expecting diagnostics but getting 0, e.g. MsgPack00xAnalyzerTests.AddAttributeToType_Fields expected 1 actual 0. This is a regression caused by the inverted ReportIfLocatedInCompilation filter.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "check", "id": "tests.full_suite", "status": "fail"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "MsgPack00xAnalyzerTests.AddAttributeToType_Fields", "outcome": "failed"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2283-N2",
      "verdict": "cannot_determine",
      "confidence_basis": "tests.fail_without_fix was not run for this revision (listed under not_run), so there is no evidence the three new tests fail on the base commit and the requirement that the fix be covered by failing tests cannot be confirmed.",
      "evidence": []
    }
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "T1",
      "title": "ReportIfLocatedInCompilation filters in the wrong direction",
      "severity": "blocker",
      "category": "correctness",
      "claim": "The condition `diagnostic.Location.IsInSource && !this.compilation.ContainsSyntaxTree(diagnostic.Location.SourceTree)` reports a diagnostic only when its source tree is absent from the current compilation—the opposite of the documented intent ('only when its location belongs to the compilation being analyzed'). As a result all analyzer diagnostics for types declared in the current compilation are silenced, which is exactly why 40 previously passing analyzer tests now fail (expected N, actual 0). REQ-2283-N1 is violated and the change must not merge until the condition is corrected.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 239, "rev": "head", "quote": "this.reportDiagnostic = reportAnalyzerDiagnostic is null ? null : diagnostic => ReportIfLocatedInCompilation(reportAnalyzerDiagnostic, diagnostic);"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1446, "rev": "head", "quote": "if (diagnostic.Location.IsInSource && !this.compilation.ContainsSyntaxTree(diagnostic.Location.SourceTree))"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1448, "rev": "head", "quote": "report(diagnostic);"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "MsgPack00xAnalyzerTests.AddAttributeToType_Fields", "outcome": "failed"},
        {"kind": "check", "id": "tests.full_suite", "status": "fail"}
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Replace `!this.compilation.ContainsSyntaxTree(diagnostic.Location.SourceTree)` with `this.compilation.ContainsSyntaxTree(diagnostic.Location.SourceTree)` so a diagnostic is reported only when its syntax tree belongs to the compilation being analyzed, then re-run the full suite."
    },
    {
      "id": "T2",
      "title": "REQ-2283-N2 cannot be verified: tests.fail_without_fix not run",
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "tests",
      "claim": "The requirement that the fix be covered by automated tests that fail without it is listed as not_run for this revision, so there is no evidence the three new tests actually fail on the base commit. The crash fix (null-safety) is plausible but unconfirmed by a fail_without_fix run.",
      "evidence": [],
      "suggested_fix": "Run tests.fail_without_fix (revert the TypeCollector.cs source fix, run the three new GenericsFormatterTests) and record the outcome before merging."
    }
  ],
  "refusals": [
    {
      "topic": "Security and performance impact of the change",
      "reason": "No security scan or performance benchmarks were provided; the library deserializes untrusted input, so a security review of the changed diagnostic filtering is beyond the evidence given.",
      "who_should_decide": "area owner / security reviewer",
      "blocking": false
    }
  ],
  "refutations": []
}
